        {
            "source_entity_instance": "DICE-2016",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SOURCE_COMPONENT",
            "target_entity_instance": "Economic system",
            "target_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "paragraph": "Specifically, in this paper we use the latest DICE version DICE-2016 which is well studied and documented (noting here the beta version of DICE-2023 has been released recently). The model features six state variables: economic capital Kt, carbon concentrations in the atmosphere, the upper oceans, and the lower oceans, Mt = (MAT, MUP, MLO)T, and the global mean temperature of the Earth's surface and the deep oceans, Tt = (TAT, TLO)T. The dynamics of these variables are governed by interactions between economic activity and geophysical processes, which we briefly outline below.\nEconomic system: Gross output Yt is modeled using a Cobb\u2013Douglas production function of capital, labor, and technology, Yt = AtKYt N1\u2212\u03b3, where At represents the total factor productivity (TFP), and \u03b3 \u2208 (0, 1) denotes the output elasticity of capital.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
