            "paragraph": "Specifically, in this paper we use the latest DICE version DICE-2016 which is well studied and documented (noting here the beta version of DICE-2023 has been released recently). The model features six state variables: economic capital Kt, carbon concentrations in the atmosphere, the upper oceans, and the lower oceans, Mt = (MAT, MUP, MLO)T, and the global mean temperature of the Earth's surface and the deep oceans, Tt = (TAT, TLO)T. The dynamics of these variables are governed by interactions between economic activity and geophysical processes, which we briefly outline below.\nTemperature module: The relationship between greenhouse gas accumulations and increased radiative forcing is described by the function: Ft = \u03b7 log2(MAT/MAT)+ Ft, which models the change in total radiative forcings from anthropogenic sources such as CO2.",
